1. Based on the FY2025 10-K, Data Center revenue surged 142% to $115.2 billion driven by Hopper and early Blackwell shipments; what is management's outlook for sustaining over 100% YoY growth in FY2026 amid potential hyperscaler capex moderation?\
\
2. The annual report highlights a 75.0% gross margin for FY2025, up 2.3 points despite $1.6 billion in inventory provisions; how do you plan to mitigate future provisions related to AI GPU transitions and maintain margins above 75%?\
\
3. In the MD&A section, purchase obligations reached $30.8 billion for inventory and capacity, primarily for Blackwell; what revenue acceleration from these commitments is expected in the next 12-18 months, and how does this impact free cash flow projections?\
\
4. Gaming segment revenue grew modestly 9% to approximately $14.3 billion in FY2025 per the 10-K; what strategies from the report's discussion on GeForce RTX 40 Series will drive a stronger recovery in FY2026 amid console cycle dynamics?\
\
5. The risk factors in the FY2025 annual report emphasize U.S. export controls impacting China sales; with Data Center representing 88% of revenue, what diversification efforts are underway to offset potential further restrictions on H100/Blackwell exports?\
\
6. R&D expenses rose 49% to $12.9 billion (9.9% of revenue) as disclosed in the 10-K; what portion of this spend is allocated to AI-specific innovations like Rubin architecture, and what ROI metrics from the MD&A justify the increase?\
\
7. Operating cash flow hit a record $64.1 billion in FY2025, per the financial statements; how will the $3.4 billion in capex and $37.7 billion in share repurchases influence ROIC, and what M&A priorities align with revenue growth goals?\
\
8. The Automotive segment achieved 55% growth to $1.7 billion in FY2025, driven by self-driving platforms; drawing from the segment analysis in the annual report, what partnerships could double this revenue by FY2027?\
\
9. Executive compensation in the proxy statement ties a significant portion to revenue and EPS targets; given the 147% EPS growth to $2.94 in FY2025, how are incentive structures evolving to align with long-term AI revenue sustainability?\
\
10. The 10-K's risk factors note customer concentration risks with top clients; with total revenue at $130.5 billion and implied reliance on a few hyperscalers, what metrics from the report indicate resilience if one major customer's spend declines by 20%?\
